data: {"state":"done","seconds":10,"summary":"I'll start by pulling up ticket #1.\n\nThis ticket is really about the failing test, so proposing a follow-up to update it is essentially the fix. I should figure out who to assign it to — the ticket's currently with andres-live, but that's a guess rather than something confirmed, so I'll flag it as a field to check rather than assume.\n\nSince the ownership of the underlying PR is ambiguous between CI, frontend, or Trov themselves, I'll avoid guessing and file the new ticket unassigned in the backlog, noting the link to the original ticket in the body so the person can assign it themselves. I'll skip setting a parent relationship since that requires both tickets to share an assignee, and show the card for confirmation before creating it."}

